  {
   "kind": "paragraph",
   "text": "The last time Anna Kovac took the sleeper from Vienna to Venice, she was nineteen and the carriages smelled of diesel and oranges. This spring she made the trip again, in a refitted cabin with a reading lamp, a folding desk and a door that locks. Nothing about the route had changed, except that people had once decided to give it up.",
